1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:03,400
Stickman was taking his usual walk home after sunset.

2
00:00:03,440 --> 00:00:06,576
The shops were closing, and the streetlights were flickering.

3
00:00:06,616 --> 00:00:10,867
He expected another quiet evening, with absolutely no surprises.

4
00:00:10,907 --> 00:00:14,016
But around the next corner, a strange glow appeared.

5
00:00:16,150 --> 00:00:18,976
A golden elevator stood in the middle of the sidewalk.

6
00:00:19,016 --> 00:00:22,424
No building surrounded it. No cables reached the roof.

7
00:00:22,464 --> 00:00:25,126
Warm light spilled out across the wet pavement.

8
00:00:25,166 --> 00:00:28,315
Stickman stepped closer, wondering who could have put it there.

9
00:00:32,150 --> 00:00:36,033
Inside, the buttons looked nothing like normal elevator buttons.

10
00:00:36,073 --> 00:00:39,390
There was a glowing zero, and even impossible floors.

11
00:00:39,430 --> 00:00:42,245
One little circle blinked as if it knew his name.

12
00:00:42,285 --> 00:00:45,166
Before he could think twice, Stickman pressed zero.

13
00:00:48,150 --> 00:00:51,265
The doors flashed, and a swirling purple tunnel appeared.

14
00:00:51,305 --> 00:00:53,894
The floor began to shake beneath his sneakers.

15
00:00:53,934 --> 00:00:56,928
He tried to step backward, but the light pulled harder.

16
00:00:56,968 --> 00:00:59,566
With a shout, he ran straight into the portal.

17
00:01:04,150 --> 00:01:07,157
Suddenly, the city was floating in every direction.

18
00:01:07,197 --> 00:01:10,921
Buildings hung upside down, and cars drifted through the sky.

19
00:01:10,961 --> 00:01:14,147
Even the roads seemed to twist into impossible shapes.

20
00:01:14,187 --> 00:01:17,985
Stickman stared in disbelief. Where had the elevator taken him?

21
00:01:20,150 --> 00:01:23,204
Then gravity changed its mind and threw him upward.

22
00:01:23,244 --> 00:01:26,406
He tumbled past flying cars and glowing windows.

23
00:01:26,446 --> 00:01:29,240
The whole city spun beneath his dangling feet.

24
00:01:29,280 --> 00:01:32,903
He needed the elevator, before the sky swallowed him forever.

25
00:01:36,150 --> 00:01:38,999
He spotted those familiar golden doors just ahead.

26
00:01:39,039 --> 00:01:42,099
With one desperate leap, he grabbed the glowing frame.

27
00:01:42,139 --> 00:01:45,476
His shoes scraped against the edge as he pulled himself in.

28
00:01:45,516 --> 00:01:48,919
The doors slammed shut, and the wild city disappeared.

29
00:01:52,150 --> 00:01:55,383
Ding! The elevator opened inside an enormous bedroom.

30
00:01:55,423 --> 00:01:58,114
A teddy bear towered over him like a mountain.

31
00:01:58,154 --> 00:02:01,119
Colorful toy blocks stretched as high as houses.

32
00:02:01,159 --> 00:02:04,658
Then, somewhere behind the toys, a tiny whistle sounded.

33
00:02:08,150 --> 00:02:10,564
A toy train came roaring around the bend.

34
00:02:10,604 --> 00:02:13,238
Only it was much bigger than Stickman expected.

35
00:02:13,278 --> 00:02:16,407
He sprinted between blocks while its headlight followed him.

36
00:02:16,447 --> 00:02:19,781
The little engine was getting closer with every second.

37
00:02:24,150 --> 00:02:27,056
There! The elevator was waiting at the end of the street.

38
00:02:27,096 --> 00:02:29,809
Stickman scrambled over the last pile of blocks.

39
00:02:29,849 --> 00:02:33,590
The locomotive thundered behind him, almost catching his shoes.

40
00:02:33,630 --> 00:02:36,689
He jumped for the doorway, and everything went golden.

41
00:02:40,150 --> 00:02:43,371
The next floor opened beneath a brilliant blue ocean.

42
00:02:43,411 --> 00:02:47,129
Somehow, Stickman could breathe in this magical underwater city.

43
00:02:47,169 --> 00:02:51,522
Glowing jellyfish floated above bridges, towers, and ancient ruins.

44
00:02:51,562 --> 00:02:54,072
For a moment, he forgot to be afraid.

45
00:02:56,150 --> 00:02:59,686
Then an enormous purple octopus rose behind the ruins.

46
00:02:59,726 --> 00:03:02,894
Its eyes narrowed, and its tentacles filled the water.

47
00:03:02,934 --> 00:03:05,789
Stickman froze as the creature blocked his way.

48
00:03:05,829 --> 00:03:09,019
One angry movement told him it was time to run.

49
00:03:12,150 --> 00:03:15,820
The octopus wrapped its tentacles around the golden elevator.

50
00:03:15,860 --> 00:03:19,462
Metal bent, sparks flashed, and the walkway began to break.

51
00:03:19,502 --> 00:03:22,981
Across the ruins, Stickman spotted a glowing blue portal.

52
00:03:23,021 --> 00:03:26,361
He made one flying leap, and escaped just in time.

53
00:03:28,150 --> 00:03:31,761
He landed among floating clocks and enormous golden gears.

54
00:03:31,801 --> 00:03:35,376
Hourglasses hung in midair, with their sand completely still.

55
00:03:35,416 --> 00:03:38,502
Far ahead, a glowing path wound through the clouds.

56
00:03:38,542 --> 00:03:41,675
This strange world had somehow stopped time itself.

57
00:03:44,150 --> 00:03:46,897
A gigantic clock hand was stuck across the path.

58
00:03:46,937 --> 00:03:50,054
Stickman planted his feet and pushed with all his strength.

59
00:03:50,094 --> 00:03:53,410
Golden sparks flew as the heavy hand began moving.

60
00:03:53,450 --> 00:03:56,701
The gears awakened, and time started ticking again.

61
00:04:00,150 --> 00:04:03,077
But starting time again came with a terrible price.

62
00:04:03,117 --> 00:04:06,719
The elevator cracked apart above a swirling cosmic storm.

63
00:04:06,759 --> 00:04:10,476
Stickman clung to the broken platform as debris flew past.

64
00:04:10,516 --> 00:04:13,135
If he fell now, no floor could save him.

65
00:04:16,150 --> 00:04:19,183
He crawled toward an open panel of wires and gears.

66
00:04:19,224 --> 00:04:22,866
A glowing crystal flickered inside the damaged mechanism.

67
00:04:22,906 --> 00:04:26,231
With shaking hands, he pushed the crystal back into place.

68
00:04:26,271 --> 00:04:29,508
The golden doors flickered, then finally lit up again.

69
00:04:32,150 --> 00:04:36,054
The repaired elevator delivered him to three magical doorways.

70
00:04:36,094 --> 00:04:39,540
One showed the ocean. Another showed a giant hourglass.

71
00:04:39,580 --> 00:04:42,662
The third doorway glowed with a tiny golden house.

72
00:04:42,702 --> 00:04:46,118
For the first time, Stickman knew exactly which to choose.

73
00:04:48,150 --> 00:04:50,236
He reached toward the bright symbol of home.

74
00:04:50,276 --> 00:04:53,838
The golden doorway burst open, flooding everything with light.

75
00:04:53,878 --> 00:04:56,462
Behind it, he could almost see his own bedroom.

76
00:04:56,502 --> 00:05:00,322
Stickman ran forward, certain the adventure was finally over.

77
00:05:04,150 --> 00:05:07,283
He stumbled onto his bedroom carpet, safe at last.

78
00:05:07,323 --> 00:05:10,129
His bed and window were just where he remembered.

79
00:05:10,169 --> 00:05:13,343
Then a quiet ding sounded from inside the wardrobe.

80
00:05:13,383 --> 00:05:16,603
He turned around. The elevator had followed him home.

81
00:05:20,150 --> 00:05:23,313
Before he could close the doors, a golden ticket appeared.

82
00:05:23,353 --> 00:05:26,222
It floated out of the elevator and stopped in midair.

83
00:05:26,262 --> 00:05:29,611
A tiny magical picture shimmered across its surface.

84
00:05:29,651 --> 00:05:33,331
Stickman reached for it, unable to resist one more mystery.

85
00:05:36,150 --> 00:05:39,470
The ticket unfolded a glowing map across his bedroom.

86
00:05:39,510 --> 00:05:42,432
It showed a shining castle above floating islands.

87
00:05:42,472 --> 00:05:46,473
Far below, a hidden world glowed with waterfalls and crystals.

88
00:05:46,513 --> 00:05:49,912
A golden path pointed directly back to the elevator.

89
00:05:52,150 --> 00:05:55,541
Stickman stepped inside, holding the ticket above his head.

90
00:05:55,581 --> 00:05:59,029
The golden elevator began descending into a hidden world.

91
00:05:59,069 --> 00:06:03,077
Through its windows, he saw ancient arches and shimmering waterfalls.

92
00:06:03,117 --> 00:06:06,013
This time, he had a mission instead of a mistake.

93
00:06:08,150 --> 00:06:11,540
The doors opened on a kingdom made from lost belongings.

94
00:06:11,580 --> 00:06:15,388
Keys, toys, umbrellas, and clocks floated above the clouds.

95
00:06:15,428 --> 00:06:18,842
In the distance, a bright lighthouse watched over everything.

96
00:06:18,882 --> 00:06:22,323
But none of these forgotten treasures had found its way home.

97
00:06:24,150 --> 00:06:27,502
A winding path of giant books led toward the lighthouse.

98
00:06:27,542 --> 00:06:31,011
Stickman stepped carefully from one floating page to another.

99
00:06:31,051 --> 00:06:34,507
Around him, teddy bears and missing letters drifted past.

100
00:06:34,547 --> 00:06:37,766
He followed the trail, searching for the return machine.

101
00:06:40,150 --> 00:06:43,285
Suddenly, a magical key shot out of the swirling air.

102
00:06:43,325 --> 00:06:46,247
Without it, the return machine could never be opened.

103
00:06:46,287 --> 00:06:49,784
Stickman jumped, stretching his fingers as far as possible.

104
00:06:49,824 --> 00:06:53,326
For one breathless moment, the key hovered beyond his reach.

105
00:06:56,150 --> 00:06:58,712
He caught the key and raced to a golden machine.

106
00:06:58,752 --> 00:07:02,419
At its center, an empty lock spun with magical energy.

107
00:07:02,459 --> 00:07:05,978
Stickman pressed the key into the lock, and the machine awakened.

108
00:07:06,018 --> 00:07:10,037
Brilliant rings began connecting every lost object to its owner.

109
00:07:12,150 --> 00:07:15,468
Across the sky, hundreds of golden doorways opened.

110
00:07:15,508 --> 00:07:19,159
Teddy bears, clocks, hats, and letters lifted into the air.

111
00:07:19,199 --> 00:07:22,258
Each lost treasure followed a shining path back home.

112
00:07:22,298 --> 00:07:25,770
Stickman watched the forgotten kingdom come alive with joy.

113
00:07:28,150 --> 00:07:31,663
At last, one final doorway opened beside the lighthouse.

114
00:07:31,703 --> 00:07:34,675
Beyond the golden light stood a familiar little house.

115
00:07:34,715 --> 00:07:38,565
The elevator waited behind him, ready for another adventure.

116
00:07:38,605 --> 00:07:41,763
But Stickman chose home, and ran toward the sunlight.

117
00:07:44,150 --> 00:07:47,191
Back in his bedroom, Stickman held the golden ticket.

118
00:07:47,231 --> 00:07:51,155
The strange elevator still waited quietly inside his wardrobe.

119
00:07:51,195 --> 00:07:54,356
He smiled, proud of every lost thing he had saved.

120
00:07:54,396 --> 00:07:57,585
Then the ticket blinked again. What floor comes next?

